# Gate 0 for kernel 7.0.0-sm8150-guacamole-rc4 (QCOMTEE/QTEE probe).
#
# Verified against device/testing/rc3/linux-postmarketos-qcom-sm8150/
# config-postmarketos-qcom-sm8150.aarch64.  Existing values:
#   TEE=y
#   QCOM_TZMEM=y
#   QCOM_TZMEM_MODE_SHMBRIDGE=y
#   QCOM_TZMEM_MODE_GENERIC is not set
#   QCOMTEE is not set
# QCOMTEE selects QCOM_TZMEM_MODE_SHMBRIDGE in drivers/tee/qcomtee/Kconfig,
# so enabling QCOMTEE does NOT change the allocator mode on this baseline:
# it is already SHM-bridge mode for QCOM_QSEECOM/UEFISECAPP.  The README's
# warning that gate 0 switches every qcom_scm user to SHM-bridge mode is
# therefore not true for rc3; the modem/ADSP/SLPI already boot with it.
#
# NOT PASSIVE BY CONFIGURATION ALONE: qcomtee is a module with a platform
# modalias (platform:qcomtee).  qcom_scm registers that platform device at
# every boot; if udev/systemd autoloads the installed module, qcomtee_probe()
# runs and issues the QTEE feature/version query.  Compiling =m does not
# itself load the module, but do not describe this fragment as passive on a
# normal udev system.  For a passive gate-0 check, keep qcomtee.ko out of the
# modules tree or boot with module_blacklist=qcomtee and load it manually
# only for the deliberate test.
CONFIG_TEE=y
CONFIG_QCOMTEE=m
CONFIG_QCOM_TZMEM_MODE_SHMBRIDGE=y
# CONFIG_QCOM_TZMEM_MODE_GENERIC is not set

